WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.220 --> 00:00:02.520
Welcome back to Outpost 3, ladies and gentlemen,

00:00:02.520 --> 00:00:06.340
and today we're diving deeper 
to confront the horrors that await us.

00:00:06.340 --> 00:00:07.520
So let's get into it.

00:00:07.520 --> 00:00:10.315
Emily is attempting to change when the candles go out.

00:00:10.320 --> 00:00:13.720
Very weird, since there's no 
wind in an underground bunker.

00:00:13.720 --> 00:00:18.180
After she relights the candle, the closet door 
opens, and she's bombarded with snakes.

00:00:18.380 --> 00:00:19.820
"Why did it have to be snakes?"

00:00:19.920 --> 00:00:23.680
Mead and Amazon Eve come to the rescue 
and chop the snakes to pieces,

00:00:23.680 --> 00:00:27.600
questioning how they got in - 
either through the sewage or ventilation system.

00:00:27.600 --> 00:00:32.300
But considering how they appeared right as Michael Langdon arrived, there's no doubt a connection.

00:00:32.300 --> 00:00:37.520
Snakes in the Bible, particularly the 
Book of Genesis, are seen as deceptive tricksters.

00:00:37.640 --> 00:00:38.820
Just like Michael.

00:00:38.980 --> 00:00:43.360
And it was a snake who convinced Eve to 
eat the forbidden fruit in the Garden of Eden.

00:00:43.360 --> 00:00:45.560
But we'll get into that a bit more later on.

00:00:45.700 --> 00:00:49.260
On the plus side, snakes make 
for good protein and great eatin'.

00:00:49.260 --> 00:00:52.620
Mallory wheels in the 
special treat to our starving patrons.

00:00:52.620 --> 00:00:55.260
Remember, they're only on half cube rations.

00:00:55.300 --> 00:00:58.660
Emily questions Venable about 
the man in her office, Michael Langdon,

00:00:58.660 --> 00:01:00.380
but before she can get a solid answer,

00:01:00.380 --> 00:01:04.740
her soup springs to life and a snake 
with a chopped off head slithers out.

00:01:04.740 --> 00:01:08.540
Holding hands, Timmy and Emily 
question how these snakes were still alive,

00:01:08.540 --> 00:01:11.440
and who the mystery man in Venable's office is.

00:01:11.560 --> 00:01:14.960
That is, before they're caught by 
Mead and quickly shuffle away.

00:01:14.960 --> 00:01:20.520
Langdon reveals himself to the members of the Outpost and exclaims that he's representing the Cooperative,

00:01:20.520 --> 00:01:25.640
that they're the last of civilized life on 
the planet and that life up above is brutal.

00:01:25.660 --> 00:01:28.400
The three other American Outposts have been run over,

00:01:28.400 --> 00:01:32.340
and they've lost contact with the 
six remaining international Outposts.

00:01:32.340 --> 00:01:35.060
But there's a fail-safe - the Sanctuary.

00:01:35.060 --> 00:01:38.800
The Sanctuary has certain 
security measures that will prevent it's overrun.

00:01:38.880 --> 00:01:43.260
If this is a crossover with season 3, 
these security measures could be witches.

00:01:43.260 --> 00:01:47.900
It's only through a rigorous questioning technique 
and interview process called "cooperating"

00:01:47.960 --> 00:01:51.280
that he'll determine who among 
them are worthy and sanctuary.

00:01:51.280 --> 00:01:53.800
A process which will take several days.

00:01:53.800 --> 00:01:55.300
And for those who don't make it?

00:01:55.380 --> 00:01:58.300
Poison in case the feral cannibals come knocking.

00:01:58.320 --> 00:02:01.820
Coco doesn't get off on the right foot 
by demanding she be chosen.

00:02:01.920 --> 00:02:05.400
After all, she paid to the Cooperative, 
she feels entitled to it.

00:02:05.520 --> 00:02:09.500
Not the best thing to be making demands 
to the guy who holds your life in his hands.

00:02:09.500 --> 00:02:11.740
Mr. Gallant is the first to be interviewed.

00:02:11.740 --> 00:02:12.980
Langdon explains that

00:02:12.980 --> 00:02:17.540
what might be seen as a good answer may 
be bad and what might be bad might be good,

00:02:17.600 --> 00:02:19.320
and that he'll know if he's lying.

00:02:19.320 --> 00:02:22.520
He first asks Gallant what his sexual orientation is.

00:02:22.520 --> 00:02:26.820
Gallant says he's gay but says 
he can still be useful for procreation.

00:02:26.820 --> 00:02:32.360
To which Langdon replies, "We have techniques for harvesting genetic material" - gross.

00:02:32.360 --> 00:02:37.760
But Langdon is interested into getting into the real nitty-gritty and questions Gallant about Nana Evie,

00:02:37.760 --> 00:02:40.320
who wanted him to be the perfect gay.

00:02:40.420 --> 00:02:43.300
Holding gay lunches, hoping Gallant would find a suitor.

00:02:43.340 --> 00:02:44.920
But Gallant doesn't want to be tamed.

00:02:45.000 --> 00:02:48.400
He shows up in leather and 
a gas mask to enjoy his bisque.

00:02:48.440 --> 00:02:49.700
"I freakin' love bisque!"

00:02:50.940 --> 00:02:52.360
Gallant makes a move on Langdon

00:02:52.360 --> 00:02:57.300
when Langdon terminates the interview, saying 
they'll continue this conversation another time.

00:02:57.360 --> 00:03:02.280
Emily tries to convince Timmy to steal 
2 rad suits and find Sanctuary on their own,

00:03:02.280 --> 00:03:03.780
but they don't know where it is.

00:03:03.780 --> 00:03:06.860
However, maybe something in 
Langdon's room will hold a clue.

00:03:06.860 --> 00:03:10.540
Notice here that Emily is trying to convince 
Timmy to do something he shouldn't,

00:03:10.640 --> 00:03:14.000
just like Eve tried to convince 
Adam to eat the forbidden fruit.

00:03:14.000 --> 00:03:16.360
Gallant seems to be playing with a snake of his own

00:03:16.360 --> 00:03:19.960
when he experiences flashes of 
naked Langdon over a pentagram.

00:03:20.080 --> 00:03:25.380
Could Langdon be some sort of Satanist, able to call on the powers of the Dead to do his bidding?

00:03:25.440 --> 00:03:30.780
After all, he's the conceived child of 
Vivien Harmon and ghost Tate Langdon from season 1,

00:03:30.780 --> 00:03:33.340
who, medium Billie Dean Howard said,

00:03:33.340 --> 00:03:37.500
a child born under those circumstances
 would be the Antichrist.

00:03:37.720 --> 00:03:43.220
And then we get another nod to season 1 - 
the Rubber Man, who Langdon is likely conjuring.

00:03:43.300 --> 00:03:47.020
Nana Evie stumbles across Gallant 
and Rubber Boy playing piggyback.

00:03:47.020 --> 00:03:51.140
Seems her grandson is being tamed - 
just not the way she expected it.

00:03:51.200 --> 00:03:54.820
He's also breaking one of 
the rules - unauthorized fornication.

00:03:54.820 --> 00:03:59.133
So, she does what any good grandmother
 would do and backstabs him by going to Mead

00:03:59.140 --> 00:04:02.500
so she can better solidify herself a spot in Sanctuary.

00:04:02.760 --> 00:04:07.120
Emily and Timmy break into Langdon's room, 
where they conveniently discover a laptop.

00:04:07.120 --> 00:04:09.740
It's almost as if Langdon wanted them to find it.

00:04:09.800 --> 00:04:13.380
And damn, the Wi-Fi reception must 
be great down here to get email.

00:04:13.520 --> 00:04:17.540
And it's also great to know that 
the Google server survived the apocalypse.

00:04:17.540 --> 00:04:20.260
We get some really awesome 
nuggets of information here,

00:04:20.260 --> 00:04:24.320
including how the Cooperative knows 
Venable has deviated from their plans,

00:04:24.520 --> 00:04:27.560
and the date, October 20th 2021,

00:04:27.900 --> 00:04:30.100
which means we're getting close to Halloween -

00:04:30.100 --> 00:04:34.600
a day that played a huge role in 
season 1, which spanned 2 episodes.

00:04:34.600 --> 00:04:37.640
We also see that plans to develop a fetus have failed,

00:04:37.820 --> 00:04:40.500
one of the overrun international Outposts was in Brazil,

00:04:40.620 --> 00:04:44.580
and that another was terminated because 
radiation contamination was found.

00:04:44.580 --> 00:04:48.120
Noticed here it says "Outposts 319 to 312",

00:04:48.200 --> 00:04:53.160
could that mean there are hundreds of Outposts, 
or does their numbering simply start at 310?

00:04:53.380 --> 00:04:57.640
Venable and Gallant have been marked as "red" - 
to be terminated after the interview.

00:04:57.800 --> 00:05:00.340
But two promising candidates are in the bunch.

00:05:00.600 --> 00:05:01.700
Timmy and Emily?

00:05:01.700 --> 00:05:06.200
They learn the rule about unauthorized fornication 
was Venable's, not the Cooperative's.

00:05:06.320 --> 00:05:10.400
I actually tried sending an email to cooperativeintelligence@gmail.com,

00:05:10.400 --> 00:05:11.800
but I didn't get anything back.

00:05:11.800 --> 00:05:14.520
Langdon confronts Venable about her secret rules.

00:05:14.600 --> 00:05:16.900
She says she got an encrypted communiqué,

00:05:16.900 --> 00:05:20.520
telling her about these new rules 
before all communication went down.

00:05:20.520 --> 00:05:23.240
But he was the one who sent all the communications.

00:05:23.240 --> 00:05:24.540
How is that possible?

00:05:24.620 --> 00:05:29.340
She chides him, telling him nothing would
be more humiliating than for a man like him to learn

00:05:29.340 --> 00:05:31.340
that a woman had more information.

00:05:31.440 --> 00:05:36.240
He says, "A man such as myself?" 
as his hands travelled to his crotch,

00:05:36.240 --> 00:05:38.720
Insinuating that he might not be a man.

00:05:38.880 --> 00:05:41.960
Venable implies he was 
one of the ones involved in the bombings.

00:05:41.960 --> 00:05:46.120
Could he be one of the Visionaries, 
the 12 elite she mentioned in episode 1?

00:05:46.120 --> 00:05:48.780
Langdon asks Venable who would be fit for salvation.

00:05:48.880 --> 00:05:52.980
Starting with Coco, Venable calls her 
a vacuous abomination of inbreeding.

00:05:53.100 --> 00:05:54.240
"This is bullshit."

00:05:54.240 --> 00:05:57.760
Langdon tells her to take off her dress 
for the physical examination.

00:05:57.880 --> 00:06:01.720
We see a huge scar along her spine, hinting at scoliosis.

00:06:01.720 --> 00:06:03.720
Likely why she walks with a cane.

00:06:03.840 --> 00:06:07.360
He tells her she didn't pass 
before they're interrupted by Mead.

00:06:07.360 --> 00:06:10.980
Mead tells Venable about Gallant 
and the Rubber Man fornicating.

00:06:11.080 --> 00:06:13.260
Langdon and Gallant must be in cahoots.

00:06:13.260 --> 00:06:16.340
Why else would Gallant 
volunteer to be the first interview?

00:06:16.340 --> 00:06:20.020
Venable tortures Gallant, asking him 
about his meetings with Langdon.

00:06:20.100 --> 00:06:24.060
But it doesn't go well, since Gallant 
likes the pain - kinky bastard.

00:06:24.240 --> 00:06:27.620
Langdon then pays him a visit, telling him 
it wasn't him in the rubber suit.

00:06:27.720 --> 00:06:32.340
Just like how Vivien thought it was her husband 
having sex with her in the rubber suit in season 1.

00:06:32.340 --> 00:06:36.660
He also tells him that Nana Evie was the one 
who ratted him out. But how would he know that?

00:06:36.660 --> 00:06:38.160
I'll get to that theory in a bit.

00:06:38.160 --> 00:06:43.680
Coco goes on a tirade about how hard it is being a youth today, because there's too many damn options.

00:06:43.860 --> 00:06:46.440
Gallant confronts Nana about why she turned him in.

00:06:46.440 --> 00:06:49.640
She wants to live, get that golden ticket out of there.

00:06:49.640 --> 00:06:54.440
Why would they let a guy like him in, who 
squandered his life away on drugs and debauchery,

00:06:54.440 --> 00:06:59.220
putting in the final blow, saying, 
"One lifetime of me is worth fifty of yours".

00:06:59.220 --> 00:07:04.020
Timmy and Emily decide that if Venable was 
lying about the rules, they can finally get it on.

00:07:04.020 --> 00:07:06.060
And of course, this guy has to watch.

00:07:06.220 --> 00:07:09.880
Gallant is lamenting his sorry state
when he's greeted by the Rubber Man,

00:07:09.880 --> 00:07:12.720
who leads him to an empty room - very romantic.

00:07:12.720 --> 00:07:16.000
Mead and Eve grab Emily and Timmy 
after their sexual tryst,

00:07:16.000 --> 00:07:20.140
while Gallant, thinking the Rubber Man 
is Langdon, kills his Nana Evie.

00:07:20.260 --> 00:07:26.140
Perhaps he'll get a spot in Sanctuary, since Langdon was so curious about Gallant's anger earlier in the episode.

00:07:26.140 --> 00:07:28.540
Only now, we've seen it to its full extent.

00:07:28.540 --> 00:07:32.140
Timmy and Emily are brought before 
Venable, where their punishment is death.

00:07:32.140 --> 00:07:37.240
They're tossed in the decontamination chamber, where Timmy uses the hose to incapacitate the guard,

00:07:37.400 --> 00:07:40.820
grabbing his gun and shooting Mead 
before Eve knocks him unconscious.

00:07:41.060 --> 00:07:45.000
Then we're left with a pretty huge reveal: 
that Mead is a synthetic,

00:07:45.080 --> 00:07:49.180
a humanoid robot oddly similar to the synths in the "Aliens" franchise

00:07:49.180 --> 00:07:53.620
and judging by Mead's reaction, 
she doesn't know she's a robot either.

00:07:53.620 --> 00:07:59.220
Perhaps this is how Langdon knew about Gallant having sex with the Rubber Man, and Venable's rules:

00:07:59.220 --> 00:08:03.700
Mead has been transmitting everything to Langdon, 
like an unsuspecting spy.

00:08:03.700 --> 00:08:05.020
That's it for this episode .

00:08:05.020 --> 00:08:07.240
If you liked it, make sure to like and subscribe.

00:08:07.440 --> 00:08:11.380
I have a few more series coming down the pipeline, 
so I hope you'll stay tuned.

00:08:11.380 --> 00:08:12.200
And remember:

00:08:12.400 --> 00:08:13.760
Daddy loves you very much.

